 was also an incompetent idiot , because he never put a order in. He was just plain mean spirited and incompetent. \\\\nAnd I think they  I think they did it on purpose because they were mean-spirited, misogynists. \\\\nThe manager finally Came over and said blah blah blah Covid blah blah blah people are quitting blah blah blah ONE CLUB SODA!!!!!!!!!! ONE HOUR!!!!!!! That was not the problem. The bartender was looking straight at me for an hour and did it on purpose because he's unprofessional and shouldn't be working at a place like Encanto that has terrible food and terrible service\\\\n     DON'T GO HERE!!! \\\\n     GO TO THE MIRAMAR. They are professional kind nice competent intelligent and service is great!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-11-20 02:20:13\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Quick Summary\\\\nHad a wonderful return to the Belmond. Excellent service, food and ambiance throughout the night. The El Encanto Dining Room is back!\\\\n\\\\nFood- 5 stars\\\\nThey also had their Free-range chicken and tomahawk displayed to the table before bringing it back to being cut (we didn't have that experience when they restaurant first reopened earlier in the pandemic, but it's returned!)\\\\n\\\\nRoasted beet salad- very good. plated well and they even separated and plated two individual dishes for my girlfriend and I\\\\n\\\\nMaple Farms Duck Breast- this was pretty good, but the star of the show was the California Surf and Turf\\\\n\\\\nCalifornia Surf and Turf- everything about this dish was phenomenal. I usually prefer ribeyes over filets, but this was one of the best filets I've ever had. Perfectly seasoned and so buttery. The oysters along with the spinach were mouth-watering as well. This was ridiculously good\\\\n\\\\nGoleta Lemon- I liked this dessert more than the Floating Island and the tacos. It's good but not memorable\\\\n\\\\nTres Leches Chocolate Tacos- I would pass on these tacos in the future. It's a good idea and good ingredients. But it's very sloppy to eat and your hands get all sticky because the chocolate shell melts on your fingers\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nService- 5 stars\\\\nPhenomenal service from our waiters. Really appreciated that they split our salad into individual plates and even nicely plated each of them. Very helpful without being overbearing. Had a wonderful birthday dinner\\\\n\\\\nAmbiance/Value- 5 stars\\\\nExcellent views from the terrace. Lovely band in the background. It doesn't get much better\\\\n\\\\nBottom Line\\\\nOne of the best cooked filets I've had. Excellent food, service and ambiance. Will be returning!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-10-30 21:29:11\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"We had a exceptional Anniversary Dinner on the Patio Terrace under the stars.  The service was wonderful and attentive.  I had the salmon and it was very tender and flavorful. We finished dinner with the Floating Island and it was delicious. I loved the fruit (blackberries and raspberries) with the meringue and ginger cookies. I was glad since I don't like custard. We also loved the Charcoal Apricot bread. Everything was very fresh and healthy.  I can't wait to return!\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"original_answer\": \"Belmond El Encanto Dining Room, located at 800 Alvarado Pl, Santa Barbara, CA, is a multi-cuisine establishment offering seafood, American (New), breakfast, brunch, and more. It is also known for its nightlife and event planning services. The business operates from 7:00 AM to 10:00 PM, throughout the week. The restaurant has an upscale and classy ambiance, offers free Wi-Fi, outdoor seating, and valet parking. However, it does not offer take-out services. The restaurant generally receives good reviews for its food and service, but there have been instances of customers experiencing poor service. Some customers praised the restaurant for its excellent food, particularly the California Surf and Turf and the Roasted Beet Salad, and its attenti