\n* Is designated with the symbol \u00ae\\n* Provides legal protection against other companies using the same name or image\\n* Is a federal and legal registration of the mark\\n* Gives the owner exclusive rights to use the mark nationwide\\n* Prevents others from using similar marks that might cause confusion among consumers\\n\\nUnregistered Trademark:\\n\\n* Does not provide strong legal protection\\n* Is not registered with the government\\n* Does not give the owner exclusive rights to use the mark nationwide\\n* May not be recognized as a trademark by courts if challenged\\n* Can only be protected under common law, which may not provide sufficient legal remedies in cases of infringement.\\n\\nSo, the main difference between a registered trademark and an unregistered trademark is that a registered trademark provides stronger legal protection and exclusive rights to the owner, while an unregistered trademark does not have the same level of legal protection and may not be recognized as a trademark by courts.\", \"target\": \"any_unsupported_span_in_original_response\", \"visible_source_sentence_ids\": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], \"source_evidence_erased\": false}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
