ink which tasted good and a little strong, just the way I like!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-11-07 15:13:53\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Rooftop bistro and Bar with great Mountain View in search of decent management. We stopped in to attend a gathering for a co workers retirement. The rooftop is spacious with a couple fireplaces and some sofas. It was a great place to relax, have a drink and still be able to move around and visit.  Drinks were ok and food was average for the prices. Erin our server was efficient, friendly and did a fabulous job waiting on us. \\\\nHowever, that is where we have to end our compliments. \\\\nI could not give more than one star due to the management of this Bistro. Victor Cortez approached us with an attitude from the minute we arrived and although I understand businesses need some policies let's listen to our customer base and evaluate situations. We did have reservations for a large group. We could not split the bill in anyway, it all had to be tallied together and paid with one credit card. \\\\nThis makes things very difficult with a large number of coworkers and people arriving at different times. Our coworker also brought a retirement cake and was informed by Victor that (we don't do cakes) and if you expect to have that cake it will be an extra charge of $4 a person. Victor also told one of our party they should leave immediately when they tried to approach him to discuss the situation. \\\\nAll of us at this gathering work in the service industry and have dealt with many customers. We were all appalled at the lack of effective management and his lack of management training. Because of this I cannot recommend this place for any party over two and not sure if anyone should come back here. \\\\nWhat I discovered here:  although a great rooftop with an awesome Mountain View it turns out to be just another mediocre poorly managed hotel bar.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-11-06 04:24:26\\\",\\\"revie